1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:03,910
So far, choreographers Renan and JEONG MIN JUN...

2
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:06,640
have been confirmed to advance to the Last Stage.

3
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:10,649
Now, we only have the announcement for the Worst Choreographer left.

4
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:11,850
Oh, my gosh.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,550
BABYZOO, Kasper, and Hash.

6
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:19,189
Out of these three, who'll be the choreographer...

7
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:21,330
to go to the final Last Stage?

8
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:25,360
I'm not named as a choreographer, so I'm just Dancer One right now.

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,560
So I'm really anxious.

10
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:30,270
It shouldn't be the end this early. I still have more to show.

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,440
I was really nervous. You never know how it'll turn out.

12
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:35,940
"Last Stage: 24H."

13
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,810
The final Worst Choreographer is...

14
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:40,810
We made a difficult decision.

15
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:44,649
The one getting up from the floor wasn't Kasper.

16
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:46,120
It was BABYZOO at first.

17
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:49,120
I guess he was nervous during the shoot, so it didn't work.

18
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,460
He blew about three takes. Just like that.

19
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:53,790
He's pretty inconsistent.

20
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:59,499
Since the other choreographers were trying so hard to dominate...

21
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:04,970
Honestly, Kasper felt a bit lacking in the film too.

22
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,969
Hash, she has great technique,

23
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:08,440
you know, great legs and stuff like that.

24
00:01:08,470 --> 00:01:10,380
I feel like that's a really cool move,

25
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:13,950
but compared to a really cool personality...

26
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:18,480
I don't think that was strong enough among ten strong characters.

27
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,820
The final Worst Choreographer...

28
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:23,490
is Hash.

29
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:24,890
It's Hash.

30
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:27,130
(Last Stage: 24H, Hash)

31
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:28,890
(Shocked)

32
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:30,500
(Reading The Room)

33
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,900
It breaks my heart.

34
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,600
I felt really desperate.

35
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,270
How did I end up for elimination?

36
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:47,410
I think there were more than two scenes...

37
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:50,380
where Hash could've stood out.

38
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,980
It looks like similar technique.

39
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:56,620
I wish it had been choreography to express...

40
00:01:56,720 --> 00:02:00,189
a different side of herself a bit more.

41
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:03,930
I don't think she properly made the given position her own.

42
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,470
But in Hash's case, she seemed a bit passive.

43
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,870
As well as knowing how they contribute to the process...

44
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,170
and knowing that it isn't as much,

45
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:16,070
does make me think they should move on...

46
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:17,580
to the elimination round.

47
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:20,210
I felt a bit restless.

48
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:27,050
Whether Kasper helped the director during the process...

49
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:29,790
or gave a lot of ideas...

50
00:02:29,890 --> 00:02:35,730
I think he should be rated highly in the process aspect.

51
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:40,599
When directing on set, he kept helping me out as a sub.

52
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,870
Kasper did. Yes.

53
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:45,000
The lip-sync idea was Kasper's, right?

54
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,070
- That's right.
- I see.

55
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,510
I want to do this.

56
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:49,770
Because I think I can make something amazing.

57
00:02:49,810 --> 00:02:52,739
I like weird and strange things in videos,

58
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:55,309
I think that especially in dance videos...

59
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:56,919
If there's anything that catches my eyes...

60
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:58,449
even if it's for a second or a breath,

61
00:02:58,450 --> 00:03:00,050
I go like, "That?"

62
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:01,449
I remember it.

63
00:03:01,450 --> 00:03:03,150
So like this. It's not dance.

64
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:04,290
So cool.

65
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:09,829
Like BABYZOO, he didn't shine at all at first,

66
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:12,999
he was the best in this video,

67
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,600
and he got a memorable position.

68
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:17,570
BABYZOO knows how to look through the lens.

69
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,740
Putting BABYZOO in the center was a divine move. Really.

70
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:22,670
His choreography with his screen presence...

71
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:24,180
kind of mashed together.

72
00:03:24,210 --> 00:03:26,440
I'm just relieved.

73
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:30,880
Results matter, but so does process, and I think they saw that.

74
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:35,290
With this, the choreographers going to the first Last Stage are...

75
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,390
choreographers Renan, JEONG MIN JUN, and Hash.

76
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:41,760
(Last Stage: 24H, The 3 Choreographers)

77
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:43,430
(Shock)

78
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,060
Why me? I think it makes no sense.

79
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:50,970
It broke my heart that I had to do such a terrible mission.

80
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:55,170
I felt really hopeless. I don't want to be eliminated.

81
00:03:55,210 --> 00:03:59,880
Only one choreographer can protect their name until the end...

82
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,550
and return here.

83
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:06,750
The final verification stage where fate is decided, Last Stage.

84
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,890
I don't want to be eliminated, even if I die.

85
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,760
I have to survive somehow.

86
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:15,090
It's elimination and survival, so I must survive and prove myself.

87
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:17,700
It begins now.

88
00:04:18,030 --> 00:04:19,759
Ready, fight.

89
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,400
(Ready, fight!)

90
00:04:30,710 --> 00:04:34,010
(Last Stage: 24H)

91
00:04:35,010 --> 00:04:39,680
Last Stage: 24H. The time limit is only 24 hours.

92
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:43,520
Three choreographers are provided with a table and chairs.

93
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:45,960
This is the last one. The last one.

94
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,760
I'm sorry. This is because of my greed.

95
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:50,730
- Having 24 hours feels too long.
- I don't think I can win this.

96
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:53,260
- This is too strong.
- Hash will survive and return.

97
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,930
I want people to go, "Oh, shit."

98
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,940
- This is really good.
- How can they do this in 24 hours?

99
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,770
It's like 15 of MIN JUN right now.

100
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:02,570
Having 15 of MIN JUN is going to be tough.

101
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,580
- I feel we're on the same page.
- Yes.

102
00:05:05,610 --> 00:05:07,750
Who'll be the choreographer to leave the stage?

103
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,450
(Last Stage: First Elimination)

104
00:05:18,390 --> 00:05:20,760
The time limit is only 24 hours.

105
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:23,899
A mission where they had to pour everything out to survive.

106
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:25,060
(24 Hours of pouring everything out to survive)

107
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,500
Last Stage: 24H.

108
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,100
The choreographer who fails to prove themselves in the end...

109
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:33,810
will be the first to be eliminated and leave this stage.

110
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:35,370
(Surprised)

111
00:05:38,510 --> 00:05:43,410
Young Director JEONG MIN JUN, who won a global competition.

112
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,919
(Go JEONG MIN JUN!)

113
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,290
Let's go. Let's go.

114
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,860
Since this could be my last stage with my survival on the line,

115
00:05:52,890 --> 00:05:54,590
I'll survive no matter what it takes.

116
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:59,300
Director Renan, who made a mark in the K-pop scene beyond Japan.

117
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,870
There's no next, this is the last.

118
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,440
I'll try to beat the works of Hash and MIN JUN.

119
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,909
(Renan is the best!)

120
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:10,070
(Let's go Renan!)

121
00:06:10,170 --> 00:06:13,810
The peak of Mega performances, the strongest Director Hash.

122
00:06:16,550 --> 00:06:17,620
(Screaming)

123
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,080
Show them. Show them.

124
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,190
This could be my last stage.

125
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:24,790
I'll prove my capabilities with an amazing performance.

126
00:06:25,990 --> 00:06:30,330
Who'll be the only Director to move on to the next stage?

127
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:32,860
Prove yourself in 24 hours.

128
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:37,000
The story of the fierce 24 hours begins now.

129
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:38,170
You guys ready?

130
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:39,670
(Ready!)

131
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:40,970
Fight.

132
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:44,440
(Highly Anticipated)

133
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,540
Good luck, everyone.

134
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,280
(Choreographers cheering endlessly for the three)

135
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:49,780
(The 3 who spent a fierce 24 hours to survive)

136
00:06:50,210 --> 00:06:53,720
(Going back through those fateful 24 hours)

137
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:56,650
It breaks my heart.

138
00:06:57,590 --> 00:07:03,760
As a Director, I'm the one sending them to the Last Stage,

139
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,500
and since I played a part in that role,

140
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:10,399
my heart is honestly very heavy.

141
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,100
(My heart is honestly very heavy.)

142
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:17,510
Koo Young didn't make eye contact with us even once.

143
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:20,910
Director Back Koo Young, please hand over the envelope.

144
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:25,220
I couldn't look them in the eye.

145
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:32,460
(Sitting down without saying a word)

146
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:35,190
This must be really hard for Koo Young too.

147
00:07:35,230 --> 00:07:37,230
The weight on his shoulders looked so heavy.

148
00:07:38,230 --> 00:07:42,230
(The three elimination candidates heading to their Directors' Rooms)

149
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:46,100
I can't understand or accept this,

150
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:51,080
but letting my emotions take over in this situation won't help.

151
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,110
I have to show them on the Last Stage.

152
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:55,810
The hurt has piled up, but my mindset is...

153
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,220
"Okay, let's show them what I've got before I go."

154
00:07:58,250 --> 00:08:02,420
I'm strong with large groups, so I'll do what I can...

155
00:08:02,450 --> 00:08:04,920
and grind my teeth to make it as cool as possible.

156
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:06,690
(Wiping the tears)

157
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:08,390
I have no time to cry.

158
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:12,600
I'll grit my teeth and prepare.

159
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:16,600
I'll show you how outstanding my directing skills are.

160
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:19,640
In the Last Stage, I'll be persistent as an earthworm...

161
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:21,140
and show you that I can survive and come back.

162
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:23,040
(Last Stage Music Production)

163
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,510
Hello.

164
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:27,510
- Hello, hello.
- Yes, hello.

165
00:08:27,550 --> 00:08:30,650
For this first mission, I went with a dark vibe.

166
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,680
(Renan's Dark Stage)

167
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:34,920
So I wanted to go with a dark vibe together.

168
00:08:34,950 --> 00:08:37,390
Like a zombie or a horror movie.

169
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:41,930
What I'm good at is acting crazy, and I wanted to fight with that.

170
00:08:42,030 --> 00:08:43,290
Because I want to win so badly.

171
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:46,300
First of all, it's all about musicality.

172
00:08:46,430 --> 00:08:50,000
I think I like expressing music in a slightly novel, eccentric way.

173
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:52,740
Something that can bring out the Wow Factor with dance.

174
00:08:52,770 --> 00:08:56,010
- Showing that source and points?
- Showing music with the body?

175
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,610
I think this is a bit important.

176
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:01,750
Even if it isn't flashy, as long as it's built up.

177
00:09:02,150 --> 00:09:04,020
I'd like some irregular sounds to be included.

178
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:05,920
Make it easier to choreograph.

179
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:08,650
When creating a performance, a lot of different things come out.

180
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:12,060
I think it's a strategy to finish the performance within 24 hours.

181
00:09:12,490 --> 00:09:14,460
- Hello.
- Hello.

182
00:09:14,730 --> 00:09:18,500
I have to get it within 24 hours, so I chose the safe bet.

183
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:23,130
The top is a burgundy shirt, the pants are white.

184
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:27,410
The legs need to be clearly seen, so I think I chose white.

185
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:31,110
The image I have in mind is a bit gross and like a horror movie.

186
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:34,410
Whether I draw a cross or an X on my face.

187
00:09:34,450 --> 00:09:38,850
No shoes with coloured stockings, and no time for a fitting.

188
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:41,520
A bit simple, but like a ghost.

189
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:43,719
I want to interpret it a bit like a Hanbok.

190
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,790
You know that Hanbok in The People in White visual.

191
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:48,990
White clothes have a lot of advantages.

192
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:52,430
They absorb all lighting colours, making the dance look more dynamic.

193
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:57,200
(Renan's Practice Room)

194
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:01,970
Ten meters wide, two meters long. Wow, the table is really big.

195
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,940
It was much bigger than I thought.

196
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,080
Ah, this won't work.

197
00:10:07,450 --> 00:10:09,310
I don't think moving it will work.

198
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:12,250
Wow, how should I use this?

199
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:14,790
Is there anything other than climbing on it?

200
00:10:15,950 --> 00:10:20,120
I do a lot of artist work, but I don't use props much.

201
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:24,500
Hash and MIN JUN have a lot of competition experience,

202
00:10:24,530 --> 00:10:27,130
I think they're strong with objects.

203
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,800
You definitely need experience with props.

204
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:32,100
I should take a completely different approach.

205
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:35,710
I'll leave the table and chairs and use them like steps.

206
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:38,980
I should melt the table into the choreography.

207
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:42,779
Then you can sit like this and come like this.

208
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:45,520
- Oh my gosh.
- What?

209
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,349
(A bit scary)

210
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:50,690
Let's create shock and fear as soon as they see it, a bit scary.

211
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:54,460
She's a bit abnormal? This is a compliment to me.

212
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:59,660
I have to make it scary, bizarre, gross like a ghost, and chilling.

213
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:03,270
Wouldn't it be fun if I was dragged like a ghost on the table?

214
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,440
(Satisfied)

215
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:09,010
I want people to feel like, "Oh, shit."

216
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:11,009
(Hash's Practice Room)

217
00:11:11,010 --> 00:11:12,040
(Surprised)

218
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:13,640
Wow, it's this big?

219
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:18,080
- If it's this big...
- It's bigger than I imagined.

220
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:20,420
It's my first time seeing a prop like this in my life.

221
00:11:20,450 --> 00:11:23,919
I don't want to keep the prop in its original shape.

222
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:27,090
Always using it like this, or like this, or like this.

223
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:30,430
- I think about this a lot.
- It won't lift?

224
00:11:31,330 --> 00:11:33,330
(Trying to lift it)

225
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:38,100
Gosh, it wouldn't move at all. I'm doomed.

226
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:42,610
Because it was bigger and heavier than the desk I had in mind,

227
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:46,410
I realised I'd need more than ten people to modify it a bit.

228
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:49,450
It was beyond my expectations that so many people had to move it.

229
00:11:50,450 --> 00:11:53,720
I thought the battle of ideas I wanted might be impossible.

230
00:11:56,650 --> 00:11:57,690
(COME HERE members arriving early)

231
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,260
But do you have a rough idea?

232
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:03,190
So, what I was trying to do was tilt this desk.

233
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:04,230
I see. Tilt it.

234
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:06,700
- And then it flips over.
- I see.

235
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:09,230
- I think we'll have to scrap that.
- It's incredibly heavy.

236
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:12,770
Looking at this, there are too many things we can't do now,

237
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,810
but I feel like people will do this a lot.

238
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:15,840
Right.

239
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,410
- Yes.
- Someone will definitely do it.

240
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,710
It's too predictable.

241
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:22,810
It's no fun if it just sits here like this from the start.

242
00:12:22,850 --> 00:12:24,720
Anyway, it's a prop mission.

243
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:25,920
But in my opinion,

244
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:29,020
I don't think anyone else will think of moving that table.

245
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:31,420
As for using the prop uniquely,

246
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:33,960
I thought I might be the only one doing it.

247
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:37,190
I had a minimum number of people doing the choreography in the front,

248
00:12:37,230 --> 00:12:40,460
and placed as many people as possible by the table.

249
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:43,030
With multiple people working together like this,

250
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:45,540
I think we found a way to do it safely.

251
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,740
- Okay, let's just try it one time.
- Okay. Seven, eight.

252
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:51,940
(Tilting the table)

253
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:55,210
Oh. It looks better than I thought.

254
00:12:55,250 --> 00:12:58,520
I didn't know you'd lift it that high. Thank you, everyone.

255
00:12:58,550 --> 00:12:59,820
Is everyone's hand okay?

256
00:12:59,850 --> 00:13:02,620
- We're fine.
- You looked awesome just now.

257
00:13:02,650 --> 00:13:04,019
It's much higher than I thought, right? No?

258
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,620
- Did it not look pretty? Exactly.
- It looks super pretty.

259
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:10,030
Because people worked together, it created the exact picture I had.

260
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:12,500
I love it.

261
00:13:12,530 --> 00:13:15,000
I was so grateful, and it was so great.

262
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:19,100
Won't I be the only one using the prop in various ways?

263
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:21,540
I feel confident about that part.

264
00:13:21,570 --> 00:13:22,570
(I'm confident.)

265
00:13:22,571 --> 00:13:24,410
(JEONG MIN JUN's Practice Room)

266
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:28,050
Wow, they prepared something truly unbelievable.

267
00:13:28,150 --> 00:13:33,150
We have to use a ten-meter desk and up to 26 chairs.

268
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:36,719
If you look on YouTube, there are tons of routines using chairs,

269
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,389
and they want us to create something even newer from this?

270
00:13:38,390 --> 00:13:40,790
That's how I felt, so I was really worried at first.

271
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:44,700
The Stories team members have never used props before,

272
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:46,860
Do we have to use it exactly as it is?

273
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:49,829
- I'm going to flip this over.
- Usually, when you think about it,

274
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:52,100
you think about dancing on top of the desk,

275
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:56,440
or going underneath it to dance, or tilting the desk a bit,

276
00:13:56,470 --> 00:13:59,210
or altering its shape slightly.

277
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:02,310
But I came up with the idea to turn the desk into a ship.

278
00:14:02,350 --> 00:14:05,020
I asked them to flip the desk over, so we made it look like a ship.

279
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,450
(Impressed)

280
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:09,950
We could make a larger ship since it's ten meters long.

281
00:14:09,990 --> 00:14:13,090
We'll turn it vertically instead of horizontally and flip it.

282
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:15,360
- He says that's a ship.
- I see.

283
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:17,629
(That's a ship?)

284
00:14:17,630 --> 00:14:22,530
The front is too flat, so it doesn't feel like a ship.

285
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,640
Should we close the front with chairs?

286
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:27,200
I think the front needs to be closed to give off that vibe.

287
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:31,010
- Like this.
- It kind of looks like a ship.

288
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:34,610
- Agreed, agreed.
- Agreed. It looks cool, right?

289
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:38,049
Ji Woong, Jae Hwan, I don't think we'll use the back section either,

290
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:39,250
so could we cover it with chairs?

291
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,520
- Okay.
- I'll try doing this like this.

292
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:42,720
That's right.

293
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:45,190
It's nice because it hides the long table in the back.

294
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,590
- This is way better.
- It really looks like a ship.

295
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:49,230
I felt like it was lacking.

296
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:52,529
Could you place five chairs outside like this?

297
00:14:52,530 --> 00:14:53,559
- Okay.
- Of course.

298
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:56,970
- We can do it. Right, everyone?
- Yes.

299
00:14:57,170 --> 00:14:58,240
Thank you.

300
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:01,640
I think we tried to make the ship look cooler,

301
00:15:01,970 --> 00:15:05,680
and I think it really upgraded the whole ship atmosphere.

302
00:15:06,910 --> 00:15:09,310
- Oh, it's totally a ship.
- This actually works.

303
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:12,780
Goodness. Awesome. Thank you so much.

304
00:15:12,950 --> 00:15:14,550
I'll try calling Ui Jeong first.

305
00:15:14,850 --> 00:15:17,190
Should we show you our props? How we used them?

306
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:18,259
- Show me the props.
- We'll show you.

307
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,460
Guess what this is.

308
00:15:19,690 --> 00:15:22,460
- What do you think it is?
- What is it? A ship? Is it a ship?

309
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:24,660
Nice.

310
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:28,630
If you look at it from a different perspective, you see things.

311
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:30,030
So because of that,

312
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:32,540
I think we'll stand out from the other choreographers.

313
00:15:33,570 --> 00:15:36,640
(Team JEONG MIN JUN done changing)

314
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,940
Will this performance turn out the way I envisioned it?

315
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:43,480
I wanted to shock people.

316
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:47,020
I want to show the gap in our performance skills.

317
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:49,620
Can we really show the concept of a "ship" well?

318
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:53,260
Since this stage is life or death,

319
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:56,160
I think the pressure to deliver is pretty high.

320
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:59,660
If we had time, we could've broken it down more...

321
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,770
and divided it up more,

322
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:04,440
but since we can't, my mind is a mess.

323
00:16:05,970 --> 00:16:07,400
A miracle will happen again.

324
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:10,540
But I don't think it'll be easy today.

325
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,180
(Sighing)

326
00:16:14,450 --> 00:16:17,010
The Last Stage is the last one.

327
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:19,950
I hope there's a next time, and that this isn't the last.

328
00:16:20,050 --> 00:16:24,990
I want to show everything I can until the very end,

329
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:26,690
so I can't be eliminated here.

330
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:31,730
It's a 24-hour mission, but I want to show them.

331
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:35,130
Even if it's 24 hours, we can do it, so I want to show them.

332
00:16:35,170 --> 00:16:38,699
- Team Hash, let's go.
- Let's go!

333
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:39,770
I'm not dying.

334
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:42,910
I can't go home.

335
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:45,380
There's still so much I've not shown,

336
00:16:45,410 --> 00:16:47,910
so I'm not going back, and I'm going to work like crazy.

337
00:16:47,950 --> 00:16:51,520
I thought of myself as a dancer recognised for my skills.

338
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:56,750
This isn't my last stage. I'll use my head and survive.

339
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:59,719
(Until the last stage)

340
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:04,090
(All three teams finished their final practice.)

341
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,460
That must really hurt, though.

342
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:07,870
I think there must've been someone here...

343
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:10,269
who was cutting it close, for sure.

344
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:13,640
Right now, the biggest weight is actually on Koo Young,

345
00:17:13,670 --> 00:17:17,310
so I feel like none of us can understand this pressure.

346
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:22,050
It's a really awkward situation for a participant to become a judge.

347
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:24,580
The situation itself. That's never happened before.

348
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:26,550
- Right. What did everyone do?
- Exactly.

349
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,720
I'm so curious.

350
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:29,720
It probably felt like a competition again.

351
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:31,920
I feel like MIN JUN will try to overpower them with force.

352
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:37,730
And surprisingly, I think Renan prepared really well.

353
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:40,130
I saw Renan's fierce determination.

354
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:42,430
When she prepares, she goes hard.

355
00:17:42,470 --> 00:17:47,040
With tables and chairs as the theme, Hash might have the advantage.

356
00:17:47,070 --> 00:17:49,010
She's always been good at utilizing things like that.

357
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:53,340
The Director who survives this will definitely be a bit different.

358
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,610
- A bit different.
- Of course.

359
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:59,750
Watching the stage, not as a survivor,

360
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:03,420
but just as a fellow Director, cheering them on,

361
00:18:03,550 --> 00:18:05,360
I think that's how we'll watch it.

362
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:07,660
We'll do a run-through.

363
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:10,859
Oh, everyone is watching.

364
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:13,400
- Yes, exactly.
- Oh, they must be nervous.

365
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:15,630
The ones in white seem to be MIN JUN's team.

366
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:19,100
It really feels like MIN JUN is going to show off his power.

367
00:18:19,170 --> 00:18:21,369
- It's 15 people, including MIN JUN.
- Gosh.

368
00:18:21,370 --> 00:18:24,410
It's 30 people. Hash has 30 people. We'll get to see a good sample.

369
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:27,440
Do you have to go for scale, or can you just use an elite team?

370
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,710
- Are they all your team members?
- Yes.

371
00:18:30,350 --> 00:18:31,750
Wow, how did they all find the time?

372
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,520
I should be up there too.

373
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:36,150
They must be even more anxious than the dancers.

374
00:18:37,150 --> 00:18:39,059
Wow, it really is huge. Wow.

375
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:41,530
So they're finally revealing how they'll use them.

376
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:43,160
The setup itself will be different.

377
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:44,360
Man, I'm curious.

378
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:46,730
It looks like Renan is going first.

379
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:49,500
Renan is barefoot. Renan is barefoot.

380
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:51,240
All the dancers are barefoot.

381
00:18:51,370 --> 00:18:53,870
Only this team is flashy, while the other two have a subdued tone.

382
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,640
You're right. It's completely different.

383
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:58,280
- Oh, this will be fun.
- Yes, it definitely will be fun.

384
00:18:58,310 --> 00:18:59,310
Wow.

385
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,949
Standing on it is crazy.

386
00:19:01,950 --> 00:19:02,950
Oh, what's that?

387
00:19:02,951 --> 00:19:04,110
I can do things like that well too.

388
00:19:04,750 --> 00:19:07,350
Wow, they're really utilizing the chairs a lot.

389
00:19:08,550 --> 00:19:11,190
Will they lift them up when they climb and pass by?

390
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,660
It looks like Renan is going all out as a player again.

391
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:16,460
Go, MIN JUN.

392
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:17,860
(Second Rehearsal: JEONG MIN JUN)

393
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:19,860
A master has appeared, a master.

394
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:23,200
He's completely in the zone. Look at his eyes.

395
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:25,300
Oh, MIN JUN's dark circles.

396
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:28,310
COME HERE versus The Stories, a bit of a battle of pride?

397
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:31,540
Yes. Both won world competitions and won domestic ones too.

398
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:34,610
Doesn't Hash seem confident?

399
00:19:34,650 --> 00:19:37,180
Yes. We have to see her expression while watching MIN JUN's stage.

400
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:41,250
- I see. Vertical.
- I figured there would be a line.

401
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,850
Are they setting it up sideways?

402
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,019
It looks like they flip it.

403
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:47,059
Are they laying it down? It's upside down.

404
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:50,760
- Hey, MIN JUN, what did you do?
- What's between the pillars?

405
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:53,430
- They'll climb the pillars.
- He thinks differently again.

406
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,330
Man, this is fun. It's so fun, we're in trouble.

407
00:19:55,370 --> 00:19:56,430
Man, MIN JUN is going to survive this.

408
00:19:56,670 --> 00:19:57,940
No, we have to keep watching.

409
00:19:57,970 --> 00:19:59,940
We don't know if that's a good choice or not.

410
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:01,370
They're doing a lot of things.

411
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:03,170
How did they set up those chairs?

412
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,510
They tied them with zip ties.

413
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:07,110
It also looks like they're making a ship.

414
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:10,180
- You're right, like a ship.
- A ship is a good idea.

415
00:20:10,450 --> 00:20:13,220
- They'll add a story.
- Come on, man.

416
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:15,220
How on earth did they come up with this idea?

417
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:18,490
- They did well.
- Renan's expression got serious.

418
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:22,260
I wondered how they thought of this, and I think my anxiety grew a lot.

419
00:20:22,390 --> 00:20:23,660
It's very JEONG MIN JUN.

420
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:28,830
I don't think there were any choreographers I felt threatened by.

421
00:20:28,870 --> 00:20:31,570
I had confidence in my own piece.

422
00:20:33,570 --> 00:20:35,470
(Final Rehearsal: Hash)

423
00:20:35,670 --> 00:20:36,910
They're barefoot here too.

424
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:38,510
Their determination is on another level, right?

425
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:39,540
I'm looking forward to this the most.

426
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,850
The 30 people here will probably be different too.

427
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:44,180
There's definitely a buff from having so many people.

428
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:45,480
Gosh, this is a real competition.

429
00:20:45,650 --> 00:20:47,180
They came out here for a competition.

430
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:50,120
They're pointing their toes and doing splits, oh my.

431
00:20:50,150 --> 00:20:53,460
Hash has so much competition experience,

432
00:20:53,490 --> 00:20:54,660
so the one to watch out for is Hash, right?

433
00:20:55,830 --> 00:20:57,030
(Hash's rehearsal begins.)

434
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:03,030
(Cheers erupting from all over)

435
00:21:03,370 --> 00:21:05,900
They killed it. They did so well, they did so well!

436
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:09,340
They pulled off this quality in 24 hours? She's a total genius.

437
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,940
(The final rehearsal performance by Hash wraps up.)

438
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:15,280
(Excited)

439
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,550
- I'll go for Hash.
- Me too.

440
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:20,180
Because her storytelling is absolutely insane.

441
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:22,450
- Is Hash not in first place?
- Yes.

442
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:25,059
Those two just lost all their momentum.

443
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:27,720
MIN JUN is looking down right now. He's Sullen MIN JUN.

444
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,660
I honestly don't think we can beat this.

445
00:21:29,990 --> 00:21:31,230
This is just too strong.

446
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:34,900
I suddenly got so nervous. I can't get eliminated here.

447
00:21:35,070 --> 00:21:37,430
Kasper told us to be confident. He said we've got this in the bag.

448
00:21:37,470 --> 00:21:39,840
INGYOO also just said we're definitely moving up.

449
00:21:40,070 --> 00:21:43,510
I just wanted to put on an amazing performance with no regrets.

450
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:46,440
I really don't want to leave. I'm just praying for a miracle.

451
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:49,710
Since our survival depends entirely on this performance,

452
00:21:49,750 --> 00:21:50,950
I'll show you that we can make it out alive.

453
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:54,350
(24-Hour countdown ends.)

454
00:21:56,750 --> 00:21:58,659
It's Street World Fighter Directors' War.

455
00:21:58,660 --> 00:22:01,690
First eliminated choreographer on...

456
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:04,830
SDF - Last Stage: 24H unfolds now.

457
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:07,230
Oh, it's really starting now.

458
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:09,830
I'm nervous and worried that I might mess up.

459
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:12,740
I think I was pretty confident in my choreography.

460
00:22:12,870 --> 00:22:17,870
Now, let's meet the Fight Judge who'll be evaluating the results.

461
00:22:17,910 --> 00:22:18,910
Who is it?

462
00:22:19,740 --> 00:22:23,210
I'm hoping for a judge with a lot of diverse experience.

463
00:22:23,350 --> 00:22:25,120
Honestly, I don't think I'll be worried no matter who it is.

464
00:22:25,150 --> 00:22:29,120
A choreographer who knows the power of performance better than anyone.

465
00:22:29,150 --> 00:22:30,720
- Who is it?
- Who could it be?

466
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:33,820
Korea's top performance director, Fight Judge Honey J.

467
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:36,060
Oh, it's Honey J.

468
00:22:36,090 --> 00:22:37,090
(Fight Judge Honey J)

469
00:22:37,860 --> 00:22:39,500
I was so happy to see her.

470
00:22:39,530 --> 00:22:41,530
It was about time she made an appearance.

471
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,700
Oh, she looked so cool.

472
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:55,710
It was so great.

473
00:22:56,010 --> 00:22:58,980
She's the winner of season one, after all.

474
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:00,980
Her aura was just so incredible.

475
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:04,289
Since she did the untouchable Mega Crew Directing,

476
00:23:04,290 --> 00:23:06,990
she's someone who has already proven herself so many times.

477
00:23:07,990 --> 00:23:13,300
I thought she was one of the judges who really stands out as a Director.

478
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,600
I have absolutely no idea what Honey J will think of it.

479
00:23:25,010 --> 00:23:27,680
She was overflowing with charisma and looked so cool.

480
00:23:27,810 --> 00:23:31,080
A creator who goes beyond movement to craft a masterpiece.

481
00:23:31,110 --> 00:23:33,220
Who is it? Who could it be?

482
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:36,390
With delicate storytelling and highly original directing,

483
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:38,290
this choreographer is capturing the attention of the entire world.

484
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,690
(This is crazy.)

485
00:23:42,390 --> 00:23:45,000
- Sean Lew.
- No way.

486
00:23:45,830 --> 00:23:48,369
Sean Lew is here. Oh my god.

487
00:23:48,370 --> 00:23:51,670
(Exclaiming)

488
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,770
We've got a real heavyweight here.

489
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,270
- Wow, it's Sean Lew.
- It was honestly so surreal.

490
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:57,310
He's so cool.

491
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,750
(Exclaiming)

492
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:05,950
It's "Red Red."

493
00:24:14,830 --> 00:24:16,529
Sean Lew is number one in the world.

494
00:24:16,530 --> 00:24:19,230
He's a battler, a choreographer,

495
00:24:19,430 --> 00:24:21,970
and he makes absolutely incredible films too.

496
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:25,470
Sean Lew is honestly just amazing at everything he does.

497
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:30,540
I didn't expect Sean Lew here,

498
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:37,510
and I was really looking forward to hearing his critiques.

499
00:24:45,290 --> 00:24:47,990
No one can argue with Sean Lew.

500
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,770
- He's so cute.
- So cute.

501
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:57,900
(Love It)

502
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,039
