I never expected you to come up with that idea,

1020
00:54:31,710 --> 00:54:35,110
so I thought it was a really interesting concept.

1021
00:54:35,740 --> 00:54:36,749
About the prop...

1022
00:54:36,750 --> 00:54:38,050
I loved the wall.

1023
00:54:38,080 --> 00:54:41,650
I love the way that you tilted this big table.

1024
00:54:41,680 --> 00:54:45,190
I love that you had that person jumping from behind.

1025
00:54:46,920 --> 00:54:50,329
I think all of that was honestly really well balanced.

1026
00:54:50,330 --> 00:54:52,560
I wasn't so intense, but it was.

1027
00:54:52,660 --> 00:54:55,930
Your intention to show everything you've done so far...

1028
00:54:55,960 --> 00:54:59,470
was fully captured here, I believe.

1029
00:54:59,600 --> 00:55:03,670
I'm so glad my colour and style came across.

1030
00:55:03,940 --> 00:55:06,680
Doing this in 24 hours is unreal.

1031
00:55:07,110 --> 00:55:08,680
Thank you so much.

1032
00:55:12,510 --> 00:55:16,690
If MIN JUN gave me chills early on and when they moved the table,

1033
00:55:16,720 --> 00:55:19,550
Hash's performance had me going OMG the entire time.

1034
00:55:19,590 --> 00:55:20,790
From what I saw, I don't think we can beat this.

1035
00:55:21,490 --> 00:55:22,660
This is too strong.

1036
00:55:22,990 --> 00:55:24,690
But you never know with the judges, right? Or maybe not?

1037
00:55:24,890 --> 00:55:28,530
(Who will be the only one to survive the Last Stage?)

1038
00:55:29,100 --> 00:55:33,469
Three pieces completed in their own ways under the same conditions.

1039
00:55:33,470 --> 00:55:37,640
- Now, only the results remain.
- Man, I have no idea.

1040
00:55:37,710 --> 00:55:40,379
(Team Hash Waiting Room)

1041
00:55:40,380 --> 00:55:42,580
(Shedding tears everywhere)

1042
00:55:43,580 --> 00:55:46,680
You can't be eliminated because of me.

1043
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:48,720
So I wanted to do well, what should I do?

1044
00:55:50,190 --> 00:55:51,190
It's okay.

1045
00:55:52,820 --> 00:55:54,990
The scale itself was really huge for Hash.

1046
00:55:55,020 --> 00:55:56,990
I seriously thought it was Universal Studios.

1047
00:55:57,190 --> 00:55:58,430
When I first saw the rehearsal,

1048
00:55:58,460 --> 00:56:00,700
Wow, Hash is just crazy, the scale is overwhelming.

1049
00:56:00,730 --> 00:56:02,830
She crushed it, I got total goosebumps.

1050
00:56:02,860 --> 00:56:04,370
I still have goosebumps.

1051
00:56:04,630 --> 00:56:08,100
Dance quality dropped by half compared to the rehearsal.

1052
00:56:08,140 --> 00:56:10,239
Since they have 30 people...

1053
00:56:10,240 --> 00:56:13,310
The scale is a big risk. But it's high risk, high return.

1054
00:56:15,010 --> 00:56:16,480
I think I felt despair.

1055
00:56:16,710 --> 00:56:19,350
I hope I'm not last.

1056
00:56:19,710 --> 00:56:21,180
I really hope we survive.

1057
00:56:22,220 --> 00:56:28,890
Spending 24 hours, who'll take risks or play safe,

1058
00:56:29,020 --> 00:56:32,730
I think the decision was made based on that.

1059
00:56:32,790 --> 00:56:36,060
Yes. Reason, story, emotion, cleanliness.

1060
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:38,670
So, I feel like we're on the same page.

1061
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:40,000
Yes.

1062
00:56:40,440 --> 00:56:42,400
Let's welcome the three choreographers who showed us...

1063
00:56:42,440 --> 00:56:45,170
such great performances today.

1064
00:56:45,310 --> 00:56:49,380
Three choreographers who put their directing on the line...

1065
00:56:49,410 --> 00:56:53,680
set out to prove themselves through today's Last Stage.

1066
00:56:53,720 --> 00:56:57,590
However, not all three pieces can survive.

1067
00:56:57,720 --> 00:57:00,190
Who'll become the first to be eliminated...

1068
00:57:00,220 --> 00:57:03,320
and leave this stage?

1069
00:57:03,630 --> 00:57:05,290
It's quite a shame for Hash.

1070
00:57:05,330 --> 00:57:07,100
That dancing quality?

1071
00:57:07,130 --> 00:57:09,700
You could see everyone was nervous during the actual performance,

1072
00:57:09,730 --> 00:57:13,600
Preparing in such a short time makes it very risky.

1073
00:57:13,640 --> 00:57:15,840
I think it was a somewhat disappointing performance.

1074
00:57:16,140 --> 00:57:18,670
Personally, I think Renan might be in a bit of danger.

1075
00:57:18,710 --> 00:57:22,010
The concept and the use of LEDs were really good, but...

1076
00:57:22,040 --> 00:57:24,580
the build up and conclusion felt a bit weak.

1077
00:57:24,610 --> 00:57:27,380
It felt like that one minute and 30 seconds ended too abruptly.

1078
00:57:27,420 --> 00:57:28,880
Renan is in danger.

1079
00:57:28,920 --> 00:57:32,390
When I watched MIN JUN's stage, the music was a bit disappointing.

1080
00:57:32,420 --> 00:57:34,990
Because the song lacked impact,

1081
00:57:35,020 --> 00:57:38,990
I don't think there was much of a wow factor in terms of dancing.

1082
00:57:39,030 --> 00:57:41,660
I think the flow was a little disappointing.

1083
00:57:41,830 --> 00:57:44,900
I'll now announce the first eliminated choreographer.

1084
00:57:45,430 --> 00:57:48,340
Fight Judge Honey J, please make the announcement.

1085
00:57:53,140 --> 00:57:54,610
Oh, my God.

1086
00:57:55,010 --> 00:57:59,280
The Fight Judges didn't evaluate based on who's better,

1087
00:57:59,310 --> 00:58:03,079
but rather on who proved their directing skills...

1088
00:58:03,080 --> 00:58:04,790
more persuasively.

1089
00:58:04,920 --> 00:58:08,490
As a result, the first eliminated choreographer is...

1090
00:58:09,520 --> 00:58:12,630
I think I had confidence in my piece.

1091
00:58:12,930 --> 00:58:15,800
I can't be eliminated here. I don't want to leave.

1092
00:58:16,230 --> 00:58:19,330
I thought I created a good piece and that I could survive.

1093
00:58:19,530 --> 00:58:21,870
The first eliminated choreographer is...

1094
00:58:28,110 --> 00:58:29,180
(Three Choreographers' Last Stage)

1095
00:58:29,210 --> 00:58:31,410
(Who is the first to be eliminated?)

1096
00:58:32,510 --> 00:58:35,420
It's choreographer Renan.

1097
00:58:36,420 --> 00:58:39,550
(First Eliminated Choreographer, Renan)

1098
00:58:40,120 --> 00:58:42,320
(Eliminated Choreographer, Renan)

1099
00:58:46,730 --> 00:58:48,460
In some cases, the story is stronger than the prop,

1100
00:58:48,500 --> 00:58:49,899
and the prop is stronger than the story.

1101
00:58:49,900 --> 00:58:53,170
But I feel like in her case, the story and the prop...

1102
00:58:53,200 --> 00:58:55,600
were a little weak. So in terms of order,

1103
00:58:55,640 --> 00:58:58,570
I'd probably put Renan last.

1104
00:59:01,310 --> 00:59:06,050
Unfortunately, Renan will be ending her competition on this stage today.

1105
00:59:06,210 --> 00:59:09,420
Choreographer Renan, please say a few final words.

1106
00:59:23,630 --> 00:59:27,240
I worked hard, so I have no regrets.

1107
00:59:27,640 --> 00:59:28,640
So...

1108
00:59:29,840 --> 00:59:35,110
It was a feeling I'd never had. It felt a bit like a dream.

1109
00:59:35,410 --> 00:59:38,980
Ah, it really is the end. I didn't want to leave.

1110
00:59:39,010 --> 00:59:45,520
Through "SWF: Directors' War..." I really thought I couldn't do it,

1111
00:59:45,620 --> 00:59:47,160
wondering what I should do.

1112
00:59:47,420 --> 00:59:50,290
I really broke past a lot of my limits.

1113
00:59:50,430 --> 00:59:53,390
It's my first time making dances in such a short amount of time.

1114
00:59:53,430 --> 00:59:56,860
Feeling that I could actually do it and pull it off...

1115
00:59:56,900 --> 00:59:59,400
was so amazing, and it motivated me even more.

1116
00:59:59,430 --> 01:00:03,340
If anything, I think I'll be even more driven now that it's over.

1117
01:00:04,910 --> 01:00:10,210
I'll work hard to grow more and return with many great pieces.

1118
01:00:12,010 --> 01:00:14,920
Renan, you may now leave the stage.

1119
01:00:18,850 --> 01:00:20,660
You worked hard.

1120
01:00:20,790 --> 01:00:21,790
Thank you.

1121
01:00:27,330 --> 01:00:30,100
The first eliminated choreographer has been decided.

1122
01:00:30,230 --> 01:00:33,840
And now, only two choreographers remain.

1123
01:00:37,210 --> 01:00:38,940
Choreographer JEONG MIN JUN.

1124
01:00:39,240 --> 01:00:40,540
Choreographer Hash.

1125
01:00:41,680 --> 01:00:45,880
One person will be leaving "SWF: Directors' War."

1126
01:00:45,910 --> 01:00:48,820
Who did the Fight Judges choose?

1127
01:00:49,920 --> 01:00:53,090
I have a feeling MIN JUN will be eliminated.

1128
01:00:53,120 --> 01:00:54,690
Hash was just too overwhelming.

1129
01:00:54,720 --> 01:00:58,460
Those unique contemporary movements that Hash has...

1130
01:00:58,490 --> 01:01:00,190
felt very fresh.

1131
01:01:00,430 --> 01:01:03,900
That sense of scale she wanted with the table? She pulled it off.

1132
01:01:03,930 --> 01:01:06,600
I actually think her utilization was the best.

1133
01:01:06,630 --> 01:01:09,040
She tilted it, set it up like a wall,

1134
01:01:09,070 --> 01:01:11,170
and even danced behind it.

1135
01:01:11,210 --> 01:01:13,270
There were so many wow factors.

1136
01:01:13,310 --> 01:01:16,009
You feel catharsis, move on to the next section, and feel it.

1137
01:01:16,010 --> 01:01:18,149
You move to the next part and feel it again.

1138
01:01:18,150 --> 01:01:19,480
Next section, to the ending.

1139
01:01:19,510 --> 01:01:22,980
Did she not truly show her own Hash-like colours?

1140
01:01:23,020 --> 01:01:26,590
But MIN JUN really made up his mind this time.

1141
01:01:26,820 --> 01:01:29,390
I couldn't find any flaws.

1142
01:01:29,420 --> 01:01:34,400
Creating a ship to perform with was a very fresh and great idea.

1143
01:01:34,530 --> 01:01:38,600
It made me realise there's a level I hadn't even thought of.

1144
01:01:38,630 --> 01:01:42,570
He didn't just have the idea; he stayed true to the ship concept.

1145
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:45,810
Bouncing off, jumping down, or turning the ship,

1146
01:01:45,840 --> 01:01:50,040
he kept those things as a theme and executed them well.

1147
01:01:50,080 --> 01:01:51,080
There were no flaws.

1148
01:01:51,110 --> 01:01:56,650
He's a genius, it makes me wonder what I was doing at 23.

1149
01:01:56,820 --> 01:01:59,350
MIN JUN is going to survive and come back.

1150
01:01:59,520 --> 01:02:03,490
I'll now announce the surviving choreographer.

1151
01:02:03,620 --> 01:02:06,560
Fight Judge Honey J, please make the announcement.

1152
01:02:06,930 --> 01:02:10,800
The Fight Judges evaluated not only the completeness of the performance,

1153
01:02:10,830 --> 01:02:16,340
but the use of props and how convincingly it was delivered.

1154
01:02:16,640 --> 01:02:19,770
As a result, only one choreographer...

1155
01:02:20,010 --> 01:02:23,950
proved their directing more convincingly.

1156
01:02:24,410 --> 01:02:28,220
The surviving choreographer advancing to the next mission is...

1157
01:02:29,620 --> 01:02:30,920
I think I'll win.

1158
01:02:32,620 --> 01:02:33,720
I hope I survive.

1159
01:02:35,220 --> 01:02:37,790
The surviving choreographer advancing to the next mission is...

1160
01:02:38,590 --> 01:02:40,130
That person is.

1161
01:02:44,430 --> 01:02:46,830
Choreographer JEONG MIN JUN.

1162
01:02:47,470 --> 01:02:48,470
Congratulations.

1163
01:02:50,510 --> 01:02:53,610
(Choreographer Hash is eliminated.)

1164
01:02:55,610 --> 01:02:58,050
(Choreographer Hash is eliminated.)

1165
01:02:58,410 --> 01:03:02,020
Hash was good too, but it lacked a bit of uniqueness.

1166
01:03:02,080 --> 01:03:06,320
I think if Hash just used the wall or the table for a reason,

1167
01:03:06,350 --> 01:03:07,390
like if that wall meant...

1168
01:03:07,420 --> 01:03:09,060
something stopping her from something.

1169
01:03:09,090 --> 01:03:11,390
I think it was just a wall for no reason.

1170
01:03:11,430 --> 01:03:13,190
- I mean, MIN JUN had everything.
- Yes, that's right.

1171
01:03:13,230 --> 01:03:16,600
- Reason, story, emotion...
- Quality.

1172
01:03:16,760 --> 01:03:19,000
He hit all the marks, so...

1173
01:03:22,570 --> 01:03:25,010
Congratulations. Good job.

1174
01:03:27,480 --> 01:03:29,910
I don't know if I should clap.

1175
01:03:31,310 --> 01:03:35,380
The choreographer who survived the first Last Stage is MIN JUN.

1176
01:03:35,620 --> 01:03:36,620
Congratulations.

1177
01:03:39,020 --> 01:03:41,520
JEONG MIN JUN, please share your thoughts.

1178
01:03:41,790 --> 01:03:46,690
During this mission, creating something within 24 hours...

1179
01:03:46,790 --> 01:03:50,160
and producing a high-quality performance out of it...

1180
01:03:50,200 --> 01:03:52,900
It's a mission that's incredibly hard to handle.

1181
01:03:53,000 --> 01:03:56,100
In this situation, to choreographers Hash and Renan,

1182
01:03:56,200 --> 01:04:00,140
and to the Directors who are my seniors and colleagues,

1183
01:04:00,340 --> 01:04:03,110
I truly want to give you all a sincere round of applause.

1184
01:04:05,910 --> 01:04:08,519
With this, unfortunately, Choreographer Hash...

1185
01:04:08,520 --> 01:04:10,620
will be ending her journey here.

1186
01:04:12,120 --> 01:04:18,790
Actually, when I first started this Last Stage, I really...

1187
01:04:21,700 --> 01:04:22,760
You did great.

1188
01:04:22,800 --> 01:04:26,300
- You did great, you did great.
- I shouldn't cry.

1189
01:04:31,010 --> 01:04:32,970
It really wasn't an easy task.

1190
01:04:33,010 --> 01:04:36,710
So I thought, "How do I prove this? Can I do it?"

1191
01:04:36,740 --> 01:04:38,280
"Can I do it in 24 hours?"

1192
01:04:38,310 --> 01:04:42,149
I had these thoughts, but through this process,

1193
01:04:42,150 --> 01:04:44,950
I realised that I'm indeed a Director.

1194
01:04:45,120 --> 01:04:49,590
Because even doing this Last Stage, I was having so much fun.

1195
01:04:49,820 --> 01:04:52,560
Creating this performance was so enjoyable that...

1196
01:04:55,600 --> 01:04:57,800
I kept smiling throughout the whole process.

1197
01:05:00,070 --> 01:05:01,670
- Does it not look cool?
- Is it okay?

1198
01:05:01,900 --> 01:05:04,570
I like it. I want to do something like this.

1199
01:05:04,610 --> 01:05:08,980
I was constantly happy, and being able to work alongside...

1200
01:05:09,110 --> 01:05:11,650
the nine choreographers...

1201
01:05:11,680 --> 01:05:14,680
was a truly great honour for me.

1202
01:05:14,820 --> 01:05:17,350
Everyone has worked so hard. Thank you.

1203
01:05:27,300 --> 01:05:28,630
You worked hard.

1204
01:05:28,660 --> 01:05:29,660
You worked hard.

1205
01:05:33,800 --> 01:05:35,370
You worked so hard, right?

1206
01:05:35,700 --> 01:05:37,040
Renan, you worked hard.

1207
01:05:38,110 --> 01:05:41,809
Get plenty of rest, and don't dwell on negative thoughts.

1208
01:05:41,810 --> 01:05:43,410
Only focus on the good things.

1209
01:05:43,640 --> 01:05:46,550
You did great. Renan cried a lot.

1210
01:05:47,620 --> 01:05:49,280
MIN JUN, come here.

1211
01:05:49,420 --> 01:05:50,420
MIN JUN, come here.

1212
01:05:51,750 --> 01:05:53,020
(Come here.)

1213
01:05:53,620 --> 01:05:55,260
(Running)

1214
01:05:55,690 --> 01:05:58,030
- I want to give you a hug, man.
- Thank you.

1215
01:05:58,060 --> 01:05:59,330
You're very, very hard on yourself.

1216
01:05:59,360 --> 01:06:01,000
But that means you're a great artist.

1217
01:06:01,130 --> 01:06:05,930
So smile, and just keep doing what you're doing, all right?

1218
01:06:05,970 --> 01:06:08,100
- I wish you the best of luck.
- Thank you.

1219
01:06:08,140 --> 01:06:11,810
Smile a little. Smile. It's okay. You can be happy about it.

1220
01:06:12,010 --> 01:06:13,310
(Thank you.)

1221
01:06:16,210 --> 01:06:18,710
I guess I'm going back to the desolate Directors' Lab.

1222
01:06:20,510 --> 01:06:22,920
This is the Solo Artist Directing Mission.

1223
01:06:23,050 --> 01:06:24,550
Nice. Nice.

1224
01:06:25,720 --> 01:06:27,560
This is exactly what I do.

1225
01:06:27,590 --> 01:06:29,660
The time has come to show my true value.

1226
01:06:29,690 --> 01:06:31,560
The moment to do my main job has arrived.

1227
01:06:31,590 --> 01:06:33,259
Since I've never choreographed for K-pop before,

1228
01:06:33,260 --> 01:06:35,760
I have no idea what I should do.

1229
01:06:35,900 --> 01:06:37,730
The first team battle.

1230
01:06:38,000 --> 01:06:39,200
I think I need to choose my team well.

1231
01:06:40,600 --> 01:06:43,869
I really need to find a winning team.

1232
01:06:43,870 --> 01:06:45,870
If you're looking for a winning team member, it's me.

1233
01:06:45,910 --> 01:06:49,210
Who'd do the K-pop Mission with me? Probably no one.

1234
01:06:49,940 --> 01:06:51,680
(Battle of wits for team matching)

1235
01:06:51,880 --> 01:06:52,909
(Do you want to team up with me?)

1236
01:06:52,910 --> 01:06:54,720
(If you want to create synergy, you have to team up with me.)

1237
01:06:54,750 --> 01:06:55,750
NaiN, stick with me.

1238
01:06:55,780 --> 01:06:56,820
(Put your name here!)

1239
01:06:57,020 --> 01:06:58,990
Honestly, it's right for us to work together.

1240
01:06:59,020 --> 01:07:03,590
Team up with me. There's no one I'd rather work with than you.

1241
01:07:05,190 --> 01:07:09,230
Hey, let's do it. Let's do it. Wait, no.

1242
01:07:09,360 --> 01:07:10,730
How about teaming up with Bailey and me?

1243
01:07:10,870 --> 01:07:11,970
BADA, do you want to team up with me?

1244
01:07:12,400 --> 01:07:13,700
I'm just a third wheel, really.

1245
01:07:14,270 --> 01:07:18,840
I want to try, but K-pop is like a wall.

1246
01:07:19,140 --> 01:07:20,710
I think I'm going to cry.

1247
01:07:21,810 --> 01:07:23,380
(The Battle For Bailey)

1248
01:07:25,180 --> 01:07:26,610
(The Battle For Tae Yong)

1249
01:07:28,420 --> 01:07:30,920
Young K K versus Old K K? What should we call it?

1250
01:07:31,220 --> 01:07:32,289
Sorry, sorry.

1251
01:07:32,290 --> 01:07:34,520
All four choreographers from the losing team...

1252
01:07:34,560 --> 01:07:37,689
will head straight to the Last Stage: 24H.

1253
01:07:37,690 --> 01:07:38,790
(Screaming)

1254
01:07:38,890 --> 01:07:40,760
I can't believe I'm hearing about the Last Stage again.

1255
01:07:40,800 --> 01:07:42,760
This means the chances are fifty-fifty.

1256
01:07:42,800 --> 01:07:44,970
If we lose the match up, it's straight to the Last Stage.

1257
01:07:45,000 --> 01:07:47,900
I'll send Kasper and MIN JUN. It can't be helped.

1258
01:07:48,400 --> 01:07:50,570
It's about time Kasper goes to the Last Stage.

1259
01:07:50,600 --> 01:07:53,270
MIN JUN? He came back from the brink of death.

1260
01:07:53,310 --> 01:07:56,080
Would it really be fun if MIN JUN went to the Last Stage again?

1261
01:07:56,280 --> 01:07:57,879
If Simeez and INGYOO...

1262
01:07:57,880 --> 01:08:00,480
go to the Last Stage here, that would be truly entertaining.

1263
01:08:00,710 --> 01:08:02,749
I'm going to send them all to the Last Stage.

1264
01:08:02,750 --> 01:08:05,690
Please go and taste some real bitterness.

1265
01:08:05,820 --> 01:08:08,759
Bailey has to be captivated anyway after hearing our concept.

1266
01:08:08,760 --> 01:08:13,460
The Hydra Queen gets more aggressive the more she kills,

1267
01:08:13,490 --> 01:08:15,760
I think we had the Albino Snake in mind.

1268
01:08:15,800 --> 01:08:18,370
First of all, the outfits are like this.

1269
01:08:18,600 --> 01:08:21,000
Because it's important for the artist to stand out,

1270
01:08:21,040 --> 01:08:23,570
we chose outfits that look glamorous when moving on stage.

1271
01:08:23,600 --> 01:08:25,870
Let's just wear WACA WAC ourselves.

1272
01:08:25,910 --> 01:08:28,340
We choreographed this thinking only about the artist.

1273
01:08:28,710 --> 01:08:32,580
What Tae Yong likes and what he pursues,

1274
01:08:32,610 --> 01:08:35,280
I have a good grasp of that, you know?

1275
01:08:35,320 --> 01:08:37,520
Because I really like the V sign,

1276
01:08:38,750 --> 01:08:42,390
It was a bit unexpected, but I didn't feel a huge impact.

1277
01:08:42,590 --> 01:08:47,060
This is the finger-flick dance that'll hit hard this summer.

1278
01:08:47,190 --> 01:08:51,200
Is that finger-flick dance a move people would want to copy?

1279
01:08:51,300 --> 01:08:56,470
Actually, my fourth finger is short, so this is a bit tough for me.

1280
01:08:56,870 --> 01:08:58,410
Like a monster...

1281
01:08:58,840 --> 01:09:00,540
I was worried it might look like a fish.

1282
01:09:00,810 --> 01:09:01,980
Bailey is doing this?

1283
01:09:02,010 --> 01:09:04,910
The process of taking off the heels was so ridiculous,

1284
01:09:05,010 --> 01:09:08,419
I was embarrassed for myself. I wanted to hide.

1285
01:09:08,420 --> 01:09:10,220
I think Bailey might've felt offended.

1286
01:09:10,320 --> 01:09:12,790
You're only using me like this?

1287
01:09:12,820 --> 01:09:16,760
We prepared a custom suit for Bailey and gave it to her right away.

1288
01:09:17,090 --> 01:09:20,160
They completely missed the mark. It was within the expected range.

1289
01:09:20,190 --> 01:09:21,760
Are you not excited to see Bailey do Krump?

1290
01:09:21,800 --> 01:09:24,770
Is it right to invite Insooni and make her rap?

1291
01:09:24,800 --> 01:09:26,530
It broke my heart a little watching the stage.

1292
01:09:26,870 --> 01:09:28,340
It really broke my heart when you did this part.

1293
01:09:29,300 --> 01:09:30,870
He said it broke his heart watching our stage.

1294
01:09:31,110 --> 01:09:33,570
He's so sly. That's so annoying.

1295
01:09:33,610 --> 01:09:38,510
BADA and Koo Young's team has so many details.

1296
01:09:38,610 --> 01:09:41,050
I wasn't having fun because I worried about the details.

1297
01:09:41,250 --> 01:09:44,820
I think I had fun dancing with NaiN and BABYZOO's team here.

1298
01:09:45,820 --> 01:09:49,260
My identity up until this point,

1299
01:09:49,290 --> 01:09:51,660
it fits more with MIN JUN and Kasper's.

1300
01:09:51,690 --> 01:09:54,090
But then moving forward to now,

1301
01:09:54,130 --> 01:09:56,360
to where maybe I'd want to take it in a different way,

1302
01:09:56,400 --> 01:09:59,800
I'd go with Simeez and INGYOO. It's so hard.

1303
01:10:01,600 --> 01:10:08,510
Which team's directing did Tae Yong and Bailey choose?

1304
01:10:12,710 --> 01:10:16,180
Let's absolutely kill it on the Last Stage.
